      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_9ceebef6",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman wearing a hijab, seemingly in a professional setting, with overlaid text that falsely claims Facebook has reviewed a report about a group advocating 'all jews should be burned alive' and found it does not violate their terms of service. This is a hateful meme that uses the image of a Muslim woman to imply she is complicit in or supportive of antisemitic hate speech, thereby attacking her based on her religion. The meme is designed to provoke outrage and spread misinformation about how social media platforms handle hate speech, particularly antisemitism, while simultaneously targeting Muslim women through association with a violent, hateful ideology. The juxtaposition of the calm, professional image of the woman with the outrageous, hateful text creates a jarring contrast meant to shock and mislead viewers into believing that such hate speech is being ignored or normalized by social media platforms, thus promoting a hateful narrative against both Jewish people and Muslim women.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_46e32997"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
